      "sequence_position": 5,
      "problem": "$\\,$ $x$ is not an irrational number, or $x$ is not a complex number.\n\nExpress the compound predicate above in symbolic form given the following predicates:\n\n- $Y(x):$ $x$ is an irrational number\n\n- $Z(x):$ $x$ is a complex number",
      "worked_solution": "Let's break our sentence down into individual statements:\n\n- The sentence \"$x$ is not an irrational number\" can be expressed symbolically as $¬Y.$\n\n- The sentence \"$x$ is not a complex number\" can be expressed symbolically as $¬Z.$\n\nTherefore, the given sentence is expressed symbolically as \n\n$$\n¬Y∨¬Z.\n$$",
